<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orontes IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 200 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Orontes IV was the last king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orontid-dynasty">Orontid dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, reigning in the late 3rd century BCE. The Seleucid king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III</a> defeated him around 200 BCE and divided Armenia between his generals Artaxias and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zariadres">Zariadres</a>. Artaxias went on to found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxiad-dynasty">Artaxiad dynasty</a> of Greater Armenia, while Zariadres ruled Sophene.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orontes-iv.jpg" alt="Orontes IV" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: J. I. Rotter (Иосиф Роттер) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yervand_IV.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
